    "note": "master — @m0saic/alpine/heatmap/v1 (the 7th Alpine template), LOCKED 2026-06-22. A matrix heatmap in the friendly white card: a rows×cols grid of rounded cells, each colored on a single-hue intensity scale (pale tint → full color), with row labels (left gutter), column labels (top), and a Less→More legend — the GitHub contribution-calendar pattern generalized to any rows×cols data. Construction: every cell / label / legend swatch is an ABSOLUTELY-PLACED tight rect packed full-canvas via placeRects on the SNAP_PX lattice (the donut/kpi model). Two bugs caught + fixed in the sandbox: (1) cells weren't snapped to the 4px lattice → SPLIT_EXCEEDS_AXIS (0-size band); fixed by snapping pitch/gap/offsets. (2) the grid was passed as the SCALED content → insetNode re-quantized the split weights → uneven cell widths (the human caught this in Layout); fixed by passing the grid as a full-canvas extraLayer (compose(EMPTY, grid)), like the line-chart plot — cells now render at exact canvas pixels, all equal width. Color scale buckets each value into `levels` steps (default 5, like GitHub): bucket 0 = empty grey, 1..N = pale→full tints. Optional in-cell values compact-format (4.5K / 1.2M) + length-aware sizing so a big number never overflows. Animation: diagonal cascade fade (top-left→bottom-right); reduceMotion → static. 6 stress variants approved (A dark · B values+violet · C green/7-levels · D wide 3×12 no-col-labels · E 7×16 static · F big-number overflow).",
